From: 许亲风 <1161352794@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:46:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] bevy_core_pipeline: only queue the tonemapping pipeline for
 HDR views

`prepare_view_tonemapping_pipelines` specialized a pipeline that targets
`ViewTarget::TEXTURE_FORMAT_HDR` (Rgba16Float) for every view, including
the non-HDR views that `TonemappingNode` skips anyway. `PipelineCache`
compiles queued pipelines eagerly, so on a WebGL2 device without
`EXT_color_buffer_float` that pipeline fails validation ("Format
Rgba16Float is not renderable") and the app panics before its first
frame.

Skip non-HDR views. `ViewNodeRunner` already treats a missing
`ViewTonemappingPipeline` component as "nothing to run for this view".

Carried as a local patch in plant-ui's vendor/registry since 2026-10-24
(see vendor/patches/README.md there); base commit 9d8f7921.
---
 crates/bevy_core_pipeline/src/tonemapping/mod.rs | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/bevy_core_pipeline/src/tonemapping/mod.rs b/crates/bevy_core_pipeline/src/tonemapping/mod.rs
--- a/crates/bevy_core_pipeline/src/tonemapping/mod.rs
+++ b/crates/bevy_core_pipeline/src/tonemapping/mod.rs
@@ -343,6 +343,13 @@ pub fn prepare_view_tonemapping_pipelines(
     >,
 ) {
     for (entity, view, tonemapping, dither) in view_targets.iter() {
+        // The pipeline always targets `ViewTarget::TEXTURE_FORMAT_HDR` and `TonemappingNode`
+        // skips non-HDR views, so only queue it for HDR views: queued pipelines compile eagerly,
+        // and on devices where `Rgba16Float` is not renderable (WebGL2 without
+        // `EXT_color_buffer_float`) that compile fails validation and panics before the first frame.
+        if !view.hdr {
+            continue;
+        }
         // As an optimization, we omit parts of the shader that are unneeded.
         let mut flags = TonemappingPipelineKeyFlags::empty();
         flags.set(
